     "id": "estimation",
     "title": "Estimating where the dock is",
     "paragraphs": [
      "An extended Kalman filter estimates the dock's ring-centre position and axis heading from the four light pixels together with the vehicle pose at the time the image was taken. Outliers are gated, the filter re-initialises when needed, and the estimate is remembered when the lights leave the image, so the vehicle can turn away and come back.",
      "The simulator's odometry arrives slowly (about 4.5 Hz) and late (about 0.25 s). A Kalman pose filter turns it into a smooth state at the control rate. An optional dead-reckoning position source makes the last metres independent of odometry drift: in tests, a 3 m position offset changed nothing, and a 5 cm/s drift broke the odometry mode but not dead reckoning."
     ]
