     "paragraphs": [
      "A guidance state machine (WAIT → SEARCH → APPROACH → TERMINAL → DOCKED, with RETRY and SAFE_STOP) uses line-of-sight guidance onto the dock axis and a speed profile with a stopping law, so the nose ends 0.5 m inside the funnel and stops.",
      "Before committing, a feasibility check asks whether a vehicle with a 2.4 m turning circle can still get onto the dock axis in time. If not, it backs out along the axis and tries again. When the dock has never been seen, the vehicle searches with a slow circle, or flies to a staging point if a rough dock position is known. When it starts beside or behind the dock, it orbits a keep-out circle on the shorter side."
     ],
     "bullets": [
      "Allocation turns the commanded wrench into thruster RPM and fin angles, with a 1/speed² schedule for the fins",
      "Station keeping holds depth, pitch, surge position and heading (heading only while there is flow over the fins)",
      "Every node goes to neutral on stale odometry, a stale detection or a depth / pitch / roll trip",
      "Every tunable lives in YAML, each with its measured effect written next to it"
     ]
