     "id": "model",
     "title": "How the model works",
     "paragraphs": [
      "For each side, a fan of rays leaves the transducer on the vehicle's belly. Each ray is marched through a terrain heightmap (0.12 m steps plus 8 bisections) and intersected with analytic 3D solids; the nearest hit wins. Acoustic shadows and layover behind objects appear on their own, with no special-case code."
     ],
     "equations": [
      "flat floor:  R = H / cos φ,   g = H · tan φ,   φ ∈ [5°, 55°]",
      "P[b] = Σ w · T · Δr · σ · Δφ · Δθ        (flat floor:  P ∝ H / (R √(R² − H²)))",
      "out = round( 65535 · clip( (10 log₁₀P + L_SL + G) / 80 dB , 0, 1 ) )"
     ],
